  "notes": "The portable C++ scenario uses only the official IEEE 1516.1 API and standard library. One federate registers an object and divests its attribute; a second federate acquires that attribute and registers a different object. It then resigns with DELETE_OBJECTS_THEN_DIVEST. The other members verify removal of the departing federate's object, continued lookup of the first object, and successful acquisition of the released attribute.",
